@NODE iNTRODUCTiON "iNTRODUCTiON OF MOVE-TO-UPLOAD VERSiON 0.2"

!!! ATTENTiON !!!

THiS TOOL iS ONLY USEFULL FOR SYSOPS WHO RUN AMi EXPRESS!

MOVE-TO-UPLOAD iS A SMALL TOOL WHiCH COPiES FiLES WiTH A SPECiAL
UPLOAD-DATE-RANGE FROM THE UPLOAD DiR iNTO ANOTHER DiRECTORY.

iMAGiNE: YOU ARE THE SYSOP OF A 5 NODE ELiTE BBS AND WANT TO TRADE
ALL YOUR NEW (0-1 DAYS OLD) FiLES TO ANOTHER BBS. YOU LOAD UP YOUR
FAVOURiTE TERMiNAL PROGRAM, LAUNCH iNTO A BBS, GO iNTO THE CONFERENCE
YOU WANT TO UPLOAD YOUR FiLES, LOAD YOUR FiLE-LiSTiNG WiTH AN EDiTOR,
SEE WHAT iS NEW, START UPLOAD FiLES AND SEARCH FOR THE FiLES iN YOUR
1.2 GiG HUGE UPLOAD-DiRECTORY. THiS COSTS A LOT OF TiME AND iT'S
ABSOLUTELY BORiNG.

MY TOOL GiVES YOU THE ULTiMATE SOLUTiON. JUST START iT FROM YOUR
WORKBENCH ViA iCON OR FROM CLi, TYPE iN THE RANGE-OF-DAYS AND MY
TOOL STARTS TO COPY ALL FiLES THAT LiES iN BETWEEN THiS RANGE TO
ANOTHER DiRECTORY. THE ONLY THiNG YOU HAVE TO DO iS NOW CLiCKiNG
ON THE FiLES AND BEGiN THEM TO UPLOAD.

ALSO iT HAS @{"FEATURES" LiNK FEATURES} THAT OTHER TOOLS DOESN'T HAVE.

@ENDNODE

@NODE FEATURES "FEATURES OF MOVE-TO-UPLOAD VERSiON 0.2"

YOU CAN TYPE iN ALL NECESSARY PATHES iNTO A SPECiAL CONFiGFiLE AND
ALL YOU HAVE TO DO iS ONLY TO TYPE iN THE DATE-RANGE. iF YOU WANT
TO USE OTHER PATHES THEN YOU CAN TYPE THEM iN ALL BY HAND AND DON'T
NEED TO CREATE ANOTHER CONFiG-FiLE. PROBABLY MOST TiME YOU WANT TO
UPLOAD FiLES ONLY FROM ONE CONFERENCE.

NOW i THiNK i GAVE YOU ENOUGH REASONS TO USE MY TOOL. HAVE FUN ANYWAYS.

@ENDNODE

@NODE iNSTALLATiON "iNSTALLATiON OF MOVE-TO-UPLOAD VERSiON 0.2"

JUST THE iCON WiTH THE MAiNPROGRAM TO YOUR FAVOURiTE DiRECTORY
AND COPY THE CONTENTS OF THE S-DiRECTORY TO YOUR DiRECTORY.

THATS ALL.

@ENDNODE

@NODE CONFiG "HOW TO EDiT THE CONFiG-FiLE OF MOVE-TO-UPLOAD V0.2 ?"

MOVE-TO-UPLOAD HAS A CONFiG-FiLE CALLED 'MTU.CFG' LOCATED iN THE
S-DiRECTORY. WHEN YOU START MOVE-TO-UPLOAD V0.2 iT WiLL ASK YOU
iF YOU WANT TO USE THE DATA FORM THE CONFiG-FiLE OR iF YOU WANT
TO TYPE iN THE DATA BY HAND.

HERE ARE THE CONTENTS OF THE CONFiG-FiLE:


 1st LiNE: ' BBS:AMiGA/DiR2 '         <-- THiS iS THE LOCATiON OF YOUR 
                                          DiR-FiLE.

 2nd LiNE  ' BBS:AMiGA/UPLOAD/ '      <-- THiS iS THE UPLOAD-DiRECTORY
                                          OF THE FiLES WHiCH SHOULD BE
                                          COPiED.

 3rd LiEN: ' DH0:MODEMTOOLS/UPLOAD '  <-- THiS iS THE PATH WHERE THE
                                          FiLES SHOULD BE COPiED TO.

 

 THAT SHOULD BE ALL FOR NOW...

@ENDNODE       

